      "text": "Muhammad Ali of Egypt began the conquest of Sudan, which was completed by 1822. This marked the beginning of Egyptian rule over Sudan."
    },
    {
      "date": "1881",
      "headline": "Mahdist Revolt",
      "text": "The Mahdist Revolt began in 1881, led by Muhammad Ahmad, who declared himself the Mahdi. This revolt aimed to overthrow the Egyptian rule and establish an Islamic state."
    },
    {
      "date": "1898",
      "headline": "Battle of Omdurman",
      "text": "The Battle of Omdurman took place in 1898, where British and Egyptian forces defeated the Mahdist forces, leading to the re-establishment of Anglo-Egyptian control over Sudan."
    },
    {
      "date": "1956-01-01",
      "headline": "Independence",
      "text": "Sudan gained independence from Anglo-Egyptian rule on January 1, 1956, becoming a sovereign nation."
    },
