      "text": "The Balfour Declaration of 1926 was issued during the Imperial Conference, stating that the United Kingdom and the Dominions were 'equal in status, in no way subordinate one to another in any aspect of their domestic or external affairs, though united by a common allegiance to the Crown.' This laid the groundwork for the modern Commonwealth."
    },
