      "headline": "London Declaration",
      "text": "The London Declaration was signed, marking the birth of the modern Commonwealth. It allowed republics and other countries to join the Commonwealth, acknowledging King George VI as the 'symbol of the free association of its independent member nations and as such the Head of the Commonwealth.'"
    },
    {
      "date": "1965",
      "headline": "Establishment of the Commonwealth Secretariat",
      "text": "The Commonwealth Secretariat was established in 1965 to facilitate consultation and cooperation among member governments and countries."
    },
    {
      "date": "1971",
      "headline": "Singapore Declaration",
      "text": "The Singapore Declaration of Commonwealth Principles was issued, setting out the core political values of the Commonwealth, including democracy, human rights, and the rule of law."
    },
    {
      "date": "1991",
      "headline": "Harare Declaration",
      "text": "The Harare Declaration was issued, reaffirming the Commonwealth's commitment to the principles of democracy and good governance."
    },
    {
      "date": "2013",
      "headline": "Commonwealth Charter",
      "text": "The Commonwealth Charter was signed by Queen Elizabeth II, consolidating the values and aspirations of the Commonwealth into a single document."
    }
  ]
}

