      "date": "0878",
      "headline": "Battle of Edington",
      "text": "In May 878, Alfred achieved a decisive victory against the Viking forces led by Guthrum at the Battle of Edington. This victory led to the Treaty of Wedmore, where Guthrum converted to Christianity."
    },
    {
      "date": "0886",
      "headline": "King of the Anglo-Saxons",
      "text": "In 886, Alfred became recognized as the King of the Anglo-Saxons after the reconquest of London. This marked the beginning of a more unified England under his rule."
    },
    {
      "date": "0893",
      "headline": "Defense Against Viking Invasions",
      "text": "Between 893 and 896, Alfred successfully defended his kingdom against renewed Viking invasions, employing a series of fortifications known as burhs."
    },
    {
      "date": "0899",
      "headline": "Death of Alfred the Great",
      "text": "Alfred the Great died on October 26, 899. He was succeeded by his son, Edward the Elder. Alfred is remembered for his military victories, educational reforms, and efforts to unify England."
    }
  ]
}

