      "text": "The French established the city of Saint-Louis on an island in the Senegal River, which became an important colonial trading post."
    },
    {
      "date": "1677",
      "headline": "French Control of Gorée Island",
      "text": "The French took control of Gorée Island, which became a significant center for the Atlantic slave trade."
    },
    {
      "date": "1895",
      "headline": "Incorporation into French West Africa",
      "text": "Senegal became part of French West Africa, a federation of eight French colonial territories in Africa."
    },
    {
      "date": "1946",
      "headline": "French Citizenship",
      "text": "Senegalese were granted French citizenship, and Senegal became an overseas territory of France."
    },
    {
      "date": "1959",
      "headline": "Formation of the Mali Federation",
      "text": "Senegal and the French Sudan (now Mali) formed the Mali Federation, which gained independence from France in 1960."
    },
    {
      "date": "1960-08-20",
      "headline": "Independence of Senegal",
      "text": "Senegal became an independent nation after the dissolution of the Mali Federation."
    },
    {
